ntation Background and Fingerprinting Driving for ASU Form I-9 Eligibility Public Service Policy Verification of Employment Employees Working Outside the State of Arizona Careers at ASU Breadcrumb Home Working at ASU Careers at ASU Rights and responsibilities The following resources provide information about employee rights and responsibilities. Know your rights (02/25). Employee rights and responsibilities under the family and medical leave act (04/16). Pay transparency nondiscrimination provision . Title IX statement . H1B Visas for DACA employees Information for ASU employees about legal screenings for H1B visas . Information about the Presidents’ Alliance DHS H-1B Modernization Rule . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. Additional resources Writing your resume ASU Career and Professional Development Services Phone: 855-278-5081 Email: Email Us (link sends email) General Information Application Issues: ASU job seekers: If you experience any issues applying or submitting your application, please submit a service ticket by 5 p.m. on the day before the requisition closes. Non-ASU job seekers: 1-855-278-5081. Monday to Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m. Arizona time. ASU Business and Finance and the Office of the Chief Financial Officer Contact us Support ASU Budget and Finance Budget Finance Payroll Budget and Finance Do business with ASU Procurement SunMart Travel U.S. Passport office Facilities Development and Management Facilities Development and Management Facilities Service Request University Real Estate Human Resources Benefits Employee Assistance Office HR Forms Jobs Safety ASU Police Emergency information Employee Health Environmental Health and Safety Insurance and Risk LiveSafe mobile app Transportation Bicycles on campus Campus shuttles General Parking information Parking Permits Parking on campus Maps